{"id": "order-halant", "category": "order", "rule": "normalize.dead-consonant", "input": "क्", "expected": "क्", "source": "docs/devanagari.md", "notes": "The virama (U+094D) suppresses the inherent vowel, making क dead."}
{"id": "order-conjunct-ksha", "category": "order", "rule": "normalize.conjunct", "input": "क्ष", "expected": "क्ष", "source": "docs/devanagari.md", "notes": "क्ष is three code points: U+0915 U+094D U+0937. Stacked or side-by-side rendering is a font choice."}
