{"id": "order-cidmap-live-keta", "category": "order", "rule": "normalize.live-consonant", "input": "केत", "expected": "केत", "source": "cidmap/data/cid_mappings.json:63", "notes": "All three consonants are live: no virama, so the inherent vowel is present."}
{"id": "reph-artha", "category": "reph", "rule": "normalize.reph", "input": "अर्थ", "expected": "अर्थ", "source": "docs/devanagari.md", "notes": "र् precedes थ and is rendered as a reph."}
{"id": "reph-karya", "category": "reph", "rule": "normalize.reph", "input": "कार्य", "expected": "कार्य", "source": "docs/devanagari.md", "notes": "र् precedes य; the ा belongs to the का aksara."}
{"id": "reph-dharma", "category": "reph", "rule": "normalize.reph", "input": "धर्म", "expected": "धर्म", "source": "docs/devanagari.md", "notes": "र् precedes म and renders as a reph above the cluster."}
{"id": "reph-nirnaya", "category": "reph", "rule": "normalize.reph", "input": "निर्णय", "expected": "निर्णय", "source": "docs/devanagari.md", "notes": "र् precedes ण; the preceding ि is a matra, not part of the reph."}
